Why It Looks Boring / "AI-Generated"

How the 5 New Repositories Solve It

1. Single Locked Palette & Font Across Every Scene (channel-profile.md)

Locking every scene to #101418 background, #F2EFE9 ink, #F2B134 gold, #4E79A7 blue, and Inter / Space Grotesk makes every video look like the exact same dark corporate slide deck. Meanwhile, bang-motion/SKILL.md explicitly bans Inter as a display font because it screams generic AI UI.

Keep #F2B134 / #101418 for the brand frame/end-card (K.endCard), but unlock topic-driven palettes & expressive typography from vox-director (9 themes), huashu-art-motion (8 palettes + 53 art cards), and code-animation-prompts (12 H-series editorial pairings).

2. Single Symmetric Easing Curve (cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1))

channel-profile.md uses a single Material-Design curve (cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)) at fixed 0.4s / 0.7s / 1.2s durations for everything. Real motion design never uses one symmetric ease for every action.

Replace with asymmetric role-based physics: expo.out (cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)) for slams, back.out(1.4) (cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1)) for sticker/card pops, MO.step(12) for stop-motion collage, power2.in (0.3s) for fast exits, and MO.spring for UI elements (bang-motion/references/techniques.md, Tenten Huashu Guide).

3. Over-Reliance on ink-gold-kit (K.backdrop, K.pin, K.word)

Calling K.backdrop(name) to swap static backgrounds behind flat K.pin labels turns a 6-minute video into a glorified slideshow ("翻页式 PPT" in huashu-art-motion/SKILL.md and bang-motion/references/anti-ppt.md).

Replace static backdrop swapping with continuous 2D/3D camera worlds (#world / CAM.track) where the camera pans, zooms, and cuts across an interconnected spatial canvas (into, settle, look, camTo, zlerp).

4. Missing 2-Shots-Per-Beat Visual Cut Rule

Scenes in storyboard.md often hold one layout for an entire 8–12s narration paragraph, causing viewer drop-off.

Enforce vox-director/SKILL.md's 3–6s shot cadence rule (<= 8s max in huashu-art-motion): every 8–10s narration beat splits into Shot A (Wide establishing + title) and Shot B (Close detail cut-in, no title) cutting mid-sentence.

5. Weak Visual QA (lint_scenes.py & qc_video.py Only Check Container Specs)

Currently, lint_scenes.py checks the 180px bottom zone, <= 7 words per label, and backdrop names, while qc_video.py checks 1920x1080@30fps, >= 5:00 duration, and K.endCard. Neither script measures motion energy, dead mid-scene gaps, text overlap every 0.25s, or visual ugliness.

Upgrade lint_scenes.py and qc_video.py with huashu-art-motion's render.py --audit (0.25s bounding-box overlap check), film_gate.py (rejects if fast-motion frames < 3.5% or if any >= 0.3s dead/blank gap exists), and mg-styles-15's 7-dimension Blind Critic Jury (rubric.md).

6. Coarse SFX Sync (fetch_sfx.py) vs. Frame-Exact Perceptual Sync

Dropping generic SFX without perceptual peak alignment makes transitions feel disconnected from the motion.

Integrate cues.json + mg-styles-15's mgaudio perceptual sync point model (whoosh peak at screen center, riser climax at cut frame, impact transient at slam frame) verified via spectrogram (--hits).

7. Zero Post-Video Learning Memory

When an animation looks bad or a mistake is fixed in one video, studio-animator and studio-visual-director start the next video with zero memory of past mistakes or winning recipes.

Implement huashu-art-motion/SKILL.md's 回流 (Experience Reflow) Protocol: after every video, write lessons to .claude/memory/mistakes_and_pitfalls.md and .claude/memory/positive_recipes.md, and auto-inject them into the agents' prompts before the next video starts.

