3. Reformed foundernotes 8-Agent Workflow & Self-Improving Loop (Sonnet Medium)

Here is how we reform the .claude/agents/ crew and scripts inside arnavh1512-source/foundernotes so every single video gets better automatically:

Step 1: Pre-Production Memory Load (studio-visual-director & studio-animator)

Before planning a new video, both agents must read:

.claude/memory/mistakes_and_pitfalls.md (every visual/timing/audio bug caught in past videos and its exact fix).

.claude/memory/positive_recipes.md (07-正面经验 — proven high-performing scene recipes, camera curves, and style pairings).

.claude/memory/production_ledger.json (fingerprints of the last 5 videos—enforcing bang-motion/SKILL.md's rule that at least 3 of 5 structural elements and 3 of 4 skin dimensions must change from the prior video).

Step 2: Voicebox Narration & Word/Pause Grid Extraction (studio-sound-engineer)

Run voicebox_server.sh + narrate.py --asr --retake 2 with the "Founder Notes Narrator" profile (speed=1.0, ~179 wpm, >= 8:00 (480.0s+) total duration) (foundernotes/CLAUDE.md).

Extract exact word-level ASR timestamps (asr_beats.py) and sentence/paragraph pause arrays (SEG >= 0.45s, PARA >= 0.80s at -30 dB via vo-pauses logic) into studio-output/<slug>/cues.json.

Step 3: Storyboard & Pre-Code Lint Gate (studio-visual-director + storyboard_lint.py)

studio-visual-director writes storyboard.md and beats.json:

3–6s Shot Cadence (<= 8s hard cap): Every 8–10s narration sentence is split into Shot A (Wide + Headline <= 7 words) + Shot B (Detail Cut-In, No Headline) cutting mid-sentence (vox-director/SKILL.md).

Concrete Noun + Verb Mandate: Every shot row must name a physical Object (Noun) + Action (Verb) + Camera Move (push, pull, glide, static, snap 0.28s, slam 0.17s, cut). Abstract buzzwords with icons are rejected (huashu-art-motion/SKILL.md).

3-Direction Style Bake-Off: Proposes 3 distinct visual compositions/styles for the key frame before full scene coding begins (huashu-art-motion/SKILL.md, vox-director/SKILL.md).

Automated storyboard_lint.py Check: Blocks coding if:

First 3 seconds is a static title card instead of an active object/hand scene.

Camera pushes in 3 shots in a row without a pull-out, glide, or angle cut.

Text-dominant shots exceed 30% of total shots or any label exceeds 7 words.

On-screen numbers do not match the spoken script in script.md (huashu-art-motion/SKILL.md).

Step 4: Poster-First Keyframe Proofing & Scene Rendering (studio-animator)

"Keyframes Before Motion" (--stills): For every scene, studio-animator first renders static keyframe PNGs at peak timestamps (--stills 0.5,2.0,4.5) and audits them against:

180px bottom subtitle safe zone (foundernotes/channel-profile.md) and 5% outer frame margin (Tenten mg-styles-15 Manual).

Grayscale contrast check (<= 25% dark pocket or >= 80% light pocket behind text per bang-motion/SKILL.md).

The style's specific "Accidental Read" failure checklist from claude-drawing-skill/SKILL.md.

Deterministic Motion & Sub-Frame Motion Blur: Scenes implement window.renderAt(t) (?export=1) and render at 1920x1080 @ 30fps with sub-frame motion blur (--mb 4 --shutter 0.5) on fast camera whip pans and slams (Tenten mg-styles-15 Manual).

Step 5: Perceptual SFX Synthesis & Audio Mastering (studio-sound-engineer + studio-editor)

Synthesize and place SFX (mgaudio / fetch_sfx.py) locked to cues.json perceptual sync points:

whoosh amplitude peak aligned to camera pan midpoint.

impact / thud transient aligned to frame 0 of MO.expoOut / slam text hits.

scribble / tick stepped at 12fps (MO.step(12)) during whiteboard/Vox annotations.

Duck ambient BGM (0.6 ratio) under Voicebox narration (1.25 ratio), burn karaoke .ass subtitles in the bottom 180px safe zone (karaoke_ass.py + assemble.py), append K.endCard(S), and normalize master audio to -14 LUFS / <= -1 dBTP (foundernotes/CLAUDE.md, Tenten mg-styles-15 Manual).

Step 6: Upgraded 5-Gate Automated QA + Blind Critic Jury (studio-reality-checker)

Upgrade lint_scenes.py, qc_video.py, and studio-reality-checker.md so no video can pass without clearing all 5 quantitative gates:

Gate 1 — 0.25s Bounding-Box & Safe-Zone Audit (lint_scenes.py + render.py --audit + subzone_gate.py): Scans every 0.25s across every scene to confirm zero text clipping, zero overlapping labels, zero critical graphics entering the bottom 180px subtitle zone, and <= 7 words per label (foundernotes/channel-profile.md, huashu-art-motion/SKILL.md).

Gate 2 — Anti-PPT & Motion Energy Gate (film_gate.py in qc_video.py): Measures optical flow / frame-to-frame delta across the assembled MP4. If fast-motion frames are < 3.5% (< 0.035), it triggers a RED LIGHT rejection for static slideshow feel (huashu-art-motion/SKILL.md).

Gate 3 — Mid-Scene Blank / Dead-Gap Detector (film_gate.py in qc_video.py): Scans every frame of the assembled MP4 for any continuous >= 0.3s (>= 9 frames @ 30fps) window of near-solid color, low edge density, or frozen dead air between narration beats. Any gap >= 0.3s triggers a RED LIGHT with exact timecodes (huashu-art-motion/SKILL.md).

Gate 4 — Acoustic Sync & Gap Check (mgaudio --hits + qc_video.py): Verifies 1920x1080@30fps, >= 5:00 duration, -14 LUFS loudness, zero dropped ASR words, and <= 1 frame (33ms) alignment between visual transients and SFX hits on the spectrogram (Tenten mg-styles-15 Manual).

Gate 5 — 2-Round Blind Critic Jury (studio-reality-checker + rubric.md): studio-reality-checker (which never writes code) inspects the 0.5s contact sheet and grades 7 dimensions (style_fidelity, concept_wow, motion_craft, typography_hierarchy, camera_rhythm, audio_sync, anti_ai_slop) on a 1–10 scale, issuing 5–10 timestamped numerical fix instructions across 2 mandatory revision rounds until the score is >= 8.0/10 (foundernotes/.claude/agents/studio-reality-checker.md, Tenten mg-styles-15 Manual).

Step 7: Post-Video Self-Improvement Reflow (deliver.py + Memory Update)

At the end of every video (and whenever you point out a flaw), studio-reality-checker updates:

.claude/memory/mistakes_and_pitfalls.md: Adds the exact failure mode, timecode, root cause, and the new automated check added to lint_scenes.py or qc_video.py so it is mechanically impossible to repeat in future videos.

.claude/memory/positive_recipes.md: Saves the highest-scoring scene code patterns and camera curves (07-正面经验) so the baseline quality ratchets up after every single video.
